# The program calls Math.max over a spread array, in tail position.
# What Link claims about the result of that call rests on the signature of Math.max. The result of native code is checked against the signature at its entry check.
# The result of the prelude function that iterates over the array in place of native code is checked against the signature too.
# Fault injection, testing=UnderstateEffects:Builtin/Math.max/KindOfResult: the signature of Math.max declares null as its only result.
# The program used to print 0 instead of 0.5 and continue.
# RUN: run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# CHECK: 0.5
# CHECK-NEXT: 0
# CHECK-NEXT: went on
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(LIE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=UnderstateEffects:Builtin/Math.max/KindOfResult
# LIE: found double in a call result
# LIE-NOT: went on
